\viewkind4\uc1\pard\fi-225\li225\sl202\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\ulnone\b0 
\par 1.\cf0  How sweet the name of  Jesus sounds
\par \pard\li225\sl202\slmult0 In a believer's ear!
\par \pard\li225\sl202\slmult0\qj It soothes our sorrows, heals our wounds,
\par \pard\li225\sl202\slmult0 And drives away our fear.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li225\sl202\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. It makes the wounded spirit whole,
\par \pard\li225\sl202\slmult0 And calms the troubled breast;
\par 'tis manna to the hungry soul,
\par And to the weary rest.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li225\sl202\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. Dear name! the rock on which I build,
\par \pard\li225\sl202\slmult0 My shield and hiding place,\tab 
\par My never-failing treasury, filled
\par With boundless stores of grace.
\par \pard\sl40\slmult0 
\par \pard\fi-225\li360\sl202\slmult0\qj\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. Jesus, my Shepherd, Husband, Friend,
\par \pard\li360\sl202\slmult0  My Prophet, Priest, and King,
\par  My Lord, my Life, my Way, my End,
\par  Accept the praise I bring.
\par \pard\li360\sl40\slmult0 
\par \pard\fi-225\li360\sl202\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5. Weak is the effort of my heart,
\par \pard\li360\sl202\slmult0  And cold my warmest thought;
\par But, when I see thee as thou art,
\par I'll praise thee as I ought.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li360\sl202\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 6\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 6.  Till then I would thy love proclaim
\par \pard\li360\sl202\slmult0  With every fleeting breath;
\par  And may the music of thy name
\par \pard          Refresh my soul in death.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\f2\fs14 
\par }

